      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-richard-the-third/sceneII_29.3/p@93246",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "THIRD CITIZEN.\nBefore the days of change, still is it so.\nBy a divine instinct men’s minds mistrust\nEnsuing danger, as by proof we see\nThe water swell before a boist’rous storm.\nBut leave it all to God. Whither away?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
